Z||000000||HAGS||01-18-2001||04:51 AM||||Is it possible to use your own vehicle as your Squad car if your a cop?  I remember seeing a Fiero police car once and I'd love to have a suped up V8 Police Fiero...im working on getting my degree now so I can goto Police Academy...the military wont take me because of a bad ear so this is my second choice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||01-18-2001||05:51 AM||||I believe the Fiero you refer to was part of a DARE program that travel to schools with an exibit, rather than a functioning patrol car.<P>Besides, If you arrested someone you would have to strap them to the hood.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||01-18-2001||09:37 AM||||And then the handcuffs might scratch the paint.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||01-18-2001||09:43 AM||||The DARE car was a confiscated car from a drug dealer. As for police using Fiero's, The Chicago Police use to have 2 Fiero GT's as Undercover police cars. They "retired" them many years ago.<P>Maybe you could work your way up to a detective and use a V-8 Fiero as the car. Paint it red with white stripes down the side? Oh wait, wrong TV show, sorry.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||01-18-2001||10:24 AM||||some PDs use all kinds of cars. Cal HP used to have Mustang GTs, Okla City use to have Cudas and Camaros, I think FLa had Camaros too. Columbus police used to use all Plymouth Reliants (good chase cars, lol) Ive also seen Jeep Cherokees, Taurus, Intrepids.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||01-18-2001||11:00 AM||||There is a Met. Green 80's mustang and a black 80's firebird that the MA state police are using to catch aggressive drivers. I see them pulling cars over all the time on RT. 24. They are getting real sneaky.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000006||My7Fieros||01-18-2001||12:29 PM||||No you cannot use your own car for a patrol car and believe me, you dont want to. And if you get hired on to a dept and bring it up you'll get laughed out the the squad room.<BR>I love my Fieros, but I also enjoy driving my 99 Crown Vic with the pretty green stripe and gold star on the side!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||01-18-2001||12:47 PM||||The "DARE" car referred to belongs to the Delhi Police Department in Cincinnati, OH. That car was confiscated from a drug dealer. There <I>is</I> a department here in California that has several Fieros they utilize as regular patrol cars though ( <A HREF="http://www.opg.org/4701/fiero/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.opg.org/4701/fiero/</A> ). The selection of the cars used us generally up to the department rather than the individual who drives it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||stsmithgt||01-18-2001||12:56 PM||||Back in about 1977, my dad was a part time deputy sheriff in Dallas county in Arkansas.  He would use his 65 Ford pick up for his patrol vehicle.  The town he lives in,(a one horse town), only had one police car at the time.  The best part was that the truck had a 351 cobra jet engine in it.  When the blue lights are flashing and the old fashion siren screeming in the grill, some people thought they could get away until they see him next to them going about 120 waving them over.  That thing was a blast to drive.||||reg||6
Z||000009||onfire||01-18-2001||02:40 PM||||I have seen a few Mustang cop cars. One was painted a metalic blue with tinted windows. You would have thought it was a teenagers car, unless he had someone pulled over.<BR>I also seen a 98 or so Volvo turbo, painted white with 4 doors no lights on top. They had someone pulled over going north on I-5 before south center.That was last year. They just keep getting sneakier (is that a word?)||||reg||1
Z||000010||mblackwell||01-18-2001||02:50 PM||||I thgink all DARE cars are confinscated.  The DARE car I see around is an old Caddy.||||reg||1
